---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FlowJourney from '../components/FlowJourney.astro';
const b=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Intelligence, with structure"><section class="product-hero"><div class="hero-overline"><span class="live-mark"></span> INTRODUCING PROJECT KRITA <span class="hero-overline-right">AN ENTERPRISE INTELLIGENCE CONCEPT</span></div><div class="hero-copy"><p class="hero-kicker reveal">Meet the intelligence layer your data has been missing.</p><h1 class="reveal">See the whole<br/><span class="hero-gradient">picture.</span></h1><p class="hero-description reveal">Your organization has the data. Krita proposes the structure to connect it—turning disconnected records into relationships, explainable answers, and decisions you can trust.</p><div class="hero-buttons reveal"><a class="button button-dark" href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span>↓</span></a><a class="button button-light" href={b+'architecture/'}>Explore the platform <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="hero-disclaimer">INTERNAL CONCEPT <span>·</span> PRODUCT VISION V0.3 <span>·</span> NOT A DEPLOYED SYSTEM</div></div><div class="hero-art" aria-label="Conceptual data points converging into a connected intelligence graph"><div class="hero-art-head"><span>DISCONNECTED DATA</span><span>KRITA INTELLIGENCE</span></div><svg viewBox="0 0 1100 490" role="img" aria-label="Data flowing from disconnected source records into a connected knowledge graph"><defs><linearGradient id="line" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0"><stop stop-color="#c8c8c8"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#a0b2ed"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#6d68e9"/></linearGradient><radialGradient id="sphere"><stop stop-color="#7e8ff0"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#5255bd"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#25245f"/></radialGradient></defs><g class="data-sources">{[[120,110],[75,230],[150,355],[275,180],[270,320]].map(([x,y],i)=><g><rect x={x-38} y={y-25} width="76" height="50" rx="10" fill="#fff" stroke="#dedee6"/><path d={`M ${x-21} ${y-8} h 40 M ${x-21} ${y+1} h 28 M ${x-21} ${y+10} h 34`} stroke="#b6b9c8" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx={x+23} cy={y-11} r="4" fill="#7776de"/></g>)}</g><g fill="none" stroke="url(#line)" stroke-width="2" opacity=".7">{[[120,110],[75,230],[150,355],[275,180],[270,320]].map(([x,y])=><path d={`M ${x+39} ${y} C 440 ${y}, 430 245, 540 245`}/>)}</g><circle cx="565" cy="245" r="66" fill="url(#sphere)"/><circle cx="565" cy="245" r="85" fill="none" stroke="#d6d6ec" stroke-dasharray="5 9"/><text x="565" y="253" font-size="30" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-weight="700">k.</text><g stroke="#8384d4" stroke-width="2" fill="none">{[[565,245,795,90],[565,245,890,160],[565,245,770,290],[565,245,955,320],[565,245,850,410],[795,90,890,160],[890,160,955,320],[770,290,850,410],[770,290,955,320],[795,90,770,290]].map(([x,y,a,c])=><line x1={x} y1={y} x2={a} y2={c}/>)}</g>{[[795,90,18],[890,160,25],[770,290,27],[955,320,23],[850,410,19]].map(([x,y,r],i)=><g><circle cx={x} cy={y} r={r} fill={i===2?'#4541a8':'#fff'} stroke="#7979c8" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx={x} cy={y} r="5" fill={i===2?'#fff':'#7470d2'}/></g>)}</svg><div class="hero-art-foot"><span>RAW INPUTS</span><span>SHARED MEANING</span><span>CONNECTED CONTEXT</span></div></div><div class="hero-bottom-line"><span>01 / OVERVIEW</span><a href="#why-krita">SCROLL TO DISCOVER ↓</a></div></section><section class="statement-section" id="why-krita"><div class="section-topline"><span class="eyebrow">THE PROBLEM</span><span class="section-index">WHY KRITA EXISTS</span></div><div class="statement-grid"><h2 class="reveal">More data.<br/><span>Less clarity.</span></h2><div class="statement-body reveal"><p>Enterprises operate across databases, files, applications and teams. Each system knows something. None sees everything.</p><p>Traditional dashboards report what happened. Krita's proposed intelligence layer helps teams understand <strong>how things are connected, why they matter, and what can happen next</strong>—without losing the evidence.</p><a class="text-link" href={b+'vision/'}>Read the product vision <span>↗</span></a></div></div><div class="problem-strip"><div><span>01 / FRAGMENTED</span><strong>Data lives in silos.</strong></div><div><span>02 / DISCONNECTED</span><strong>Relationships stay hidden.</strong></div><div><span>03 / UNEXPLAINED</span><strong>Answers lack context.</strong></div></div></section><FlowJourney/><section class="platform-section"><div class="section-topline"><span class="eyebrow">ONE PLATFORM. MULTIPLE DOMAINS.</span><span class="section-index">PRODUCT FAMILY</span></div><div class="platform-heading reveal"><h2>Built once.<br/><em>Understood everywhere.</em></h2><p>Krita Core is designed as a domain-independent foundation. Industry-specific ontologies adapt it to different kinds of enterprise data.</p></div><div class="product-grid"><a class="product-card core-card" href={b+'architecture/'}><span class="product-card-top"><span>01 / FOUNDATION</span><span>↗</span></span><div class="core-art"><span class="core-ring ring-a"></span><span class="core-ring ring-b"></span><span class="core-ring ring-c"></span><span class="core-glyph">k.</span></div><div class="product-card-bottom"><span class="product-status">PROPOSED ARCHITECTURE</span><h3>Krita Core</h3><p>The shared engine for ingestion, ontology, relationships, policy and governed AI.</p><span class="product-link">Explore the foundation ↗</span></div></a><a class="product-card pulse-card" href={b+'products/pulse/'}><span class="product-card-top"><span>02 / HEALTHCARE</span><span>↗</span></span><div class="pulse-art"><div class="pulse-line"></div><span class="pulse-node p1"></span><span class="pulse-node p2"></span><span class="pulse-node p3"></span><span class="pulse-node p4"></span><span class="pulse-node p5"></span><div class="pulse-pulse">+</div></div><div class="product-card-bottom"><span class="product-status">SYNTHETIC BROWSER DEMO</span><h3>Krita Pulse</h3><p>Connect patients, encounters and operational evidence through a healthcare ontology.</p><span class="product-link">Explore Pulse ↗</span></div></a><a class="product-card ledger-card" href={b+'products/ledger/'}><span class="product-card-top"><span>03 / FINANCIAL SERVICES</span><span>↗</span></span><div class="ledger-art"><div class="ledger-bars"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><span class="ledger-orb"></span></div><div class="product-card-bottom"><span class="product-status">PLANNED DOMAIN</span><h3>Krita Ledger</h3><p>Investigate accounts, transactions, entities and risk relationships with traceable context.</p><span class="product-link">Explore Ledger ↗</span></div></a></div></section><section class="architecture-teaser"><div class="architecture-teaser-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">UNDER THE HOOD</span><h2>Powerful thinking.<br/><em>Disciplined execution.</em></h2><p>The proposed design separates AI planning from application authority. PostgreSQL holds canonical truth; a derived graph supports exploration; policies govern every request.</p><a class="button button-dark" href={b+'architecture/'}>Explore solution architecture ↗</a></div><div class="architecture-mini"><div class="arch-block">DATA SOURCES <span>CSV · SQL · APIs</span></div><div class="arch-connector">↓</div><div class="arch-block highlight">KRITA CORE <span>Ontology · Canonical store · Policy</span></div><div class="arch-connector">↓</div><div class="arch-block">INTELLIGENCE <span>Graph · Governed tools · Evidence</span></div><div class="arch-connector">↓</div><div class="arch-block">RESPONSIBLE ACTION <span>Approvals · Audit · Traceability</span></div></div></section><section class="closing-section"><span class="eyebrow">THE NEXT CHAPTER</span><h2>Make complexity<br/><em>make sense.</em></h2><p>Explore the architecture, follow the data, and see the future of governed enterprise intelligence.</p><div class="hero-buttons"><a class="button button-white" href={b+'architecture/'}>View the architecture ↗</a><a class="button button-outline-white" href={b+'product-preview/'}>Explore the studio ↗</a></div></section></Base>
